What:		/sys/class/nx-gzip/nx-gzip/cop_type
		/sys/class/ibm-power9-nv-nx-gzip/ibm-power9-nv-nx-gzip/cop_type
		/sys/class/ibm-power9-nv-nx-842/ibm-power9-nv-nx-842/cop_type
		/sys/class/ibm-power9-nv-nx-sym/ibm-power9-nv-nx-sym/cop_type
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	linuxppc-dev@lists.ozlabs.org
Description:	read only
		The VAS coprocessor type number that a send window opened
		through the class's device node binds to, in decimal: 1 for
		nx-842, 3 for nx-gzip and 5 for nx-sym.

		A class of this name exists for each node userspace may open
		a window through, named after the node under /dev/crypto.
		An engine may have more than one: nx-gzip is the node and
		the interface that existed before this kernel, and the
		ibm-power9-nv- names are this platform's own, where anything
		added since is offered.

		Each engine also has a high priority receive FIFO, which the
		switchboard serves before the normal one and which the
		kernel's own requests use; a window opened through a
		-hipri node competes with them, so such a node is meant to
		be granted deliberately rather than by default.

		A node exists only where the device tree described a receive
		FIFO of its coprocessor type, so the set present on a machine
		says what that machine has. PowerNV may have nx-gzip,
		ibm-power9-nv-nx-gzip, ibm-power9-nv-nx-842,
		ibm-power9-nv-nx-sym and a -hipri node for each of the three;
		PowerVM has nx-gzip.
		Documentation/arch/powerpc/vas-api.rst describes the nodes.

What:		/sys/class/nx-gzip/nx-gzip/req_max_processed_len
		/sys/class/ibm-power9-nv-nx-gzip/ibm-power9-nv-nx-gzip/req_max_processed_len
		/sys/class/ibm-power9-nv-nx-842/ibm-power9-nv-nx-842/req_max_processed_len
		/sys/class/ibm-power9-nv-nx-sym/ibm-power9-nv-nx-sym/req_max_processed_len
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	linuxppc-dev@lists.ozlabs.org
Description:	read only
		The largest number of bytes one request pasted through a
		window of this type may process, in decimal, or 0 when no
		limit is configured and the engine accepts any length its
		request format can express. On PowerNV all three types
		publish 0. On PowerVM the nx-gzip value is the limit the
		hypervisor reports, which is also published as
		/sys/devices/vio/ibm,compression-v1/nx_gzip_caps/req_max_processed_len.
Users:		tools/testing/selftests/powerpc/nx-gzip (gzfht_test, nx_gzip_stress)
